The complete, runnable code is [SnakeLadderDemo.java](reference-code/learning/kb/snakeladder/SnakeLadderDemo.java). It replays both worked examples and the board validations.

[![The game applies movement policy before resolving a jump.](lessons/lld-17-flow.svg)](lessons/lld-17-flow.svg)

## Closing answer

"I model a Board with a size and a map of jumps – snakes and ladders are the same Jump record, a snake just goes down. The board is validated when it's built: jumps must be on the board, not start on the last cell, have unique starts, and never end where another starts, so there are no chains or loops. Dice is an interface, with RandomDice for play and FixedDice for tests and replays. Game keeps a queue of players and their positions; each turn rolls, moves, stays put if the roll would overshoot the last cell, applies at most one jump, and either declares the winner or puts the player at the back of the queue. Each turn returns a Move record for the UI and logs."
